# Auto-deploy to Render

When the user asks for UI/backend fixes or features in this Flask desktop project (`E:\centralized-db-system`):

1. Implement the change.
2. **Without waiting to be asked**, commit the relevant files and `git push origin main` so Render auto-deploys.
3. Tell the user the commit hash and to hard-refresh after ~1–2 minutes.

## Commit / push rules

- Only stage files related to the change (no secrets, no `dist/`, build artifacts, or unrelated untracked junk).
- Use a clear conventional commit message (`fix:`, `feat:`, etc.).
- Do **not** force-push.
- Android / `Nexora20` work stays in the Android chat/workspace — do not mix unless the user explicitly asks in this chat.

## Exception

If push fails (auth/network), report the error and the local commit hash so the user can push manually.
